Z||000000||grinthock||09-13-2001||05:55 PM||||You all know the CRAP I have been goin through.... HEre is a short story<P>Car ran rich, glowing manifolds, replaced cracked manifold, wires, plugs, cap, rotor, confirmed IAC operation.<P><BR>NOW the car runs like CRAP when it's cold, and anywhere under 2K RPM.  When I mean bad I mean BAD, it back fires once or twice till it's been running for a bit.<P>I was thinking CAT clogged, any ideaS?<BR><P>------------------<BR> <A HREF="http://www.fieroworld.com" TARGET=_blank> <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/uploads/fieroworldbanner.gif"> </A> <BR>Fieroworld!  Home of my 87 GT and 85 GT<BR>Justin C.<BR>Engineer, Designer and<BR>Technical Trainer for Nortel Networks Business Products.||||reg||1
Z||000001||Sootah||09-13-2001||07:00 PM||||If your exaust was that hot then the Cat may have partially melted, restricting a lot of exaust flow. I'd just pull it out and replace with a pipe, be sure to keep it for emissions inspections. Unless you don't have them there. We don't down here in southern Utah.<P>------------------<BR>  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/halfpole.gif">   <BR><I>Never pull your pants down in Cosco, the dang monkeys will getcha</I> <BR><B>AIM</B>: KSSouter||||reg||1
